WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:04.830
After Warner Bros. unleashed two and a half
minutes of glorious Joker footage in early

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:10.040
April 2019, fans picked apart each scene,
analyzed every frame, and watched the whole

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.299
thing — multiple times and in slow-motion
— in efforts to catch every subtle reference

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.919
to pop culture and to Batman comics past.

00:00:15.919 --> 00:00:19.520
People picked up on the wink at The King of
Comedy with Robert De Niro's casting as a

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.199
talk show host, the parallel to a classic
Joker costume in the teaser's final shots,

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.260
and the allusion to another famous pale-faced
icon, Charlie Chaplin, with the banners hanging

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.740
outside Wayne Hall.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.590
What most may not have noticed the first,
second, or tenth time around is that the Joker

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.800
teaser also includes what could be an Easter
egg for the Riddler, a longtime foe of Batman.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.230
At the 57-second mark of the footage, during
the scene in which Joaquin Phoenix's Arthur

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:48.710
Fleck is standing in an elevator at Arkham
State Hospital, viewers can spot green-ink

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.410
graffiti on the wall behind him.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:54.950
Though the tag doesn't appear to hold any
deeper meaning, that punctuation mark is intriguing,

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:59.120
as it's the insignia of Edward Nygma, better
known as the Riddler.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.250
Fans are beginning to think that this could
mean the Riddler is hiding in the shadows

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.560
of director Todd Phillips' version of Gotham
City.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.610
One of the famous baddies in the Dark Knight's
rogues gallery, the Riddler has spent a ton

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:15.170
of time locked up in Arkham Asylum — seemingly
reimagined for Joker as Arkham State Hospital,

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.900
which apparently counts Arthur Fleck as a
regular visitor.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:23.000
That this sneaky green question mark appears
not just anywhere but on an elevator in Gotham's

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.180
home for the criminally insane adds some credence
to the idea that the graffiti could be a legitimate

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.010
Riddler Easter egg, and could portend an appearance
by Nygma himself.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.750
That would, unquestionably, be an awesome
surprise …

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.990
“Was that over the top?

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:41.070
I can never tell."

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.420
It wouldn't be the only clever nod to Batman
comics featured in the new Joker footage — or

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.560
the only one included in connection with Arkham
State Hospital.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.451
Just after the camera sweeps across Gotham
City in the first few seconds, the teaser

00:01:52.451 --> 00:01:57.010
shows Phoenix's Arthur sitting opposite a
social worker, played by Sharon Washington.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.760
Her name tag reveals that her name is Debra
Kane.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.240
If that surname sounds familiar, it's because
it's the same one as Batman co-creator Bob

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.970
Kane and as Batman's cousin Kate Kane, otherwise
known as Batwoman.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:12.910
There are a few other names revealed in the
trailer that could be meaningful — or not.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.520
For example, there's street sign that reads
"Jerome Avenue."

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.710
The DC television series Gotham features a
character named Jerome Valeska, who is a precursor

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:25.360
to the Joker, much like Arthur Fleck is the
man who eventually becomes the clownish criminal

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.060
in the upcoming Joker movie.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.650
Then there's the existence of Holmes Pharmacy,
which appears 10 seconds into the teaser,

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.490
when Arthur is walking down the street.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:37.310
Batman is known as the world's greatest detective
— and so is Sherlock Holmes.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:41.990
With a little mental gymnastics, one could
deduce that Joker including a pharmacy seemingly

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:46.290
named for the other best fictional crime-solver
on the planet might tease how Arthur's life

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.610
connects with Bruce Wayne's.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:51.770
Or maybe the production designer just liked
the look of the name "Holmes" on the sign!

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:55.710
Taking all this into account, it's clear how
easy it is to make something out of what very

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:56.870
well could be nothing.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:01.650
The green question mark inked on the Arkham
State Hospital elevator is certainly interesting,

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.819
but whether it's actually a Riddler Easter
egg is anyone's guess.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:05.819
Could it be?

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:06.819
Sure!

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.880
Might it just be Todd Phillips wanting to
tip his hat to the comics while keeping Joker

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.280
its own outside-of-the-DCEU thing?

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.410
Absolutely!

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.240
The beauty of this uncertainty is that fans
now have yet another reason to look forward

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.010
to Joker — beyond what looks to be a bang-up
performance by Phoenix.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.510
When the film opens in theaters on October
4th, all questions shall be answered and all

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.959
potential Easter eggs will, hopefully, be
followed up on.

